<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
        The two XML colours the app has, and both of them are the same one on
        purpose: Ink.i950 from ui/theme/Color.kt, which is ZipperColors.bgBase.

        A cold start hands the screen over three times — splash window, then the
        Activity window, then the first Compose frame. splash_bg was #0D0D0D and
        the window was AppCompat's default, so those handovers were three
        slightly different darks in a row and read as a flicker. Keeping all
        three on one value makes the launch look like nothing happened, which is
        what a launch should look like.

        If Ink.i950 ever changes in Color.kt, change it here too — the resource
        system cannot see a Kotlin constant, so this is a copy that has to be
        kept by hand.
    -->
    <color name="splash_bg">#FF070812</color>
    <color name="window_bg">#FF070812</color>
</resources>
